{
  "body_human_readable": "In a dramatic conclusion to the 2024-25 NBA season, the Oklahoma City Thunder defeated the Indiana Pacers in Game 7 of the NBA Finals to secure their first championship since the franchise relocated from Seattle. The decisive game, held on Sunday, June 22, 2025, ended with a 103-91 victory for the Thunder on their home court.\n\nThe series MVP was Oklahoma City's superstar, Shai Gilgeous-Alexander. In the final game, Gilgeous-Alexander delivered a stellar performance with 29 points and a playoff career-high 12 assists. He was instrumental throughout the series, capping off a season where he was also the league MVP.\n\nThe game and the series were a hard-fought battle. The Pacers held a narrow 48-47 lead at halftime in Game 7, despite losing their star Tyrese Haliburton to a right Achilles injury in the first quarter. However, the Thunder dominated the third quarter, outscoring the Pacers 34-20, and maintained their lead to clinch the title. Jalen Williams supported the effort with 20 points, while Chet Holmgren added 18 points and five blocks. For the Pacers, Bennedict Mathurin stepped up with 24 points and 13 rebounds in Haliburton's absence.\n\nThis championship victory marked the first in Oklahoma City's history and was the culmination of a dominant season where the team won an NBA-best 68 games during the regular season. The Thunder, the second-youngest team to win an NBA title, were celebrated for their league-leading defense and perseverance.\n\nThe full results for the seven-game series were as follows:\n*   **Game 1:** Pacers 111, Thunder 110\n*   **Game 2:** Thunder 123, Pacers 107\n*   **Game 3:** Pacers 116, Thunder 107\n*   **Game 4:** Thunder 111, Pacers 104\n*   **Game 5:** Thunder 120, Pacers 109\n*   **Game 6:** Pacers 108, Thunder 91\n*   **Game 7:** Thunder 103, Pacers 91",
  "request": {
